<title>TAIWAN: Philips auctions Taiwan Semicon shares.</title>
<headline>Philips auctions Taiwan Semicon shares.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Taiwan, a subsidiary of Philips Electronics NV, on Tuesday auctioned 51.32 million shares of microchip giant Taiwan Semiconductor at an average price of T$150.24 per share.</p>
<p>Auction prices ranged between T$149 and T$155, an official at the Taiwan Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The exchange said Philips would try to auction off 48.68 million more shares on Wednesday, bringing the total number of auctioned shares to 100 million.</p>
